; dev: the development build vscsirs.device (stock kickstart: the C driver
; runs the system disk; vscsirs.device takes the test controller, units 0
; t0, 1 t1-4k, 2 t2-3t, 3 the CD, 4 t3-fs). WRITES UNITS 0-2 and 4.
; 1. Checked random I/O on units 0-2 WITH a controller reset every 2 s.
; 2. Ten rounds of vscsitest on units 0-2 then an expunge, free memory after
;    each (the drop-in cannot expunge: only this build can show it).
;   Execute SHARED:sbench/dev
FailAt 30
MakeDir SHARED:sbench/out >NIL:
Copy SHARED:sbench/vscsirs.device DEVS: QUIET
Copy SHARED:sbench/vscsitest RAM: QUIET
Copy SHARED:sbench/expunge RAM: QUIET
Protect RAM:vscsitest +rwed QUIET
Protect RAM:expunge +rwed QUIET
Version DEVS:vscsirs.device FULL >SHARED:sbench/out/dev-version.txt
RAM:vscsitest TORTURE vscsirs.device 60 0,1,2 8 >SHARED:sbench/out/dev-torture.txt
RAM:expunge DEVICE vscsirs.device >NIL:
Echo "start" >SHARED:sbench/out/dev-expunge.txt
Set n 0
Lab round
RAM:vscsitest vscsirs.device 3 5 >RAM:dv.out
Search RAM:dv.out "tests passed" NONUM >>SHARED:sbench/out/dev-expunge.txt
Search RAM:dv.out "FAIL" NONUM >>SHARED:sbench/out/dev-expunge.txt
RAM:expunge DEVICE vscsirs.device >>SHARED:sbench/out/dev-expunge.txt
Avail FLUSH >NIL:
Avail TOTAL >>SHARED:sbench/out/dev-expunge.txt
Set n `Eval $n + 1`
If VAL $n LT 10
  Skip round BACK
EndIf
Echo "== results"
Search SHARED:sbench/out/dev-torture.txt "torture:" NONUM
Search SHARED:sbench/out/dev-torture.txt "FAIL" NONUM
Search SHARED:sbench/out/dev-expunge.txt "tests passed" NONUM
Echo "dev done" >SHARED:sbench/out/dev.done
